On Tue, Sep 25, 2001 at 01:33:04PM +0200, Thorsteinn Sveinsson wrote:
> Is there any way to get openbsd 2.9 or 3.0 to use the adaptec 2940
> controller that is shipped with it ?
> It seems to find it but says it is not configured !

By "find" I am not sure what you mean.  The Miata SRM firmware will not
reconize any Adaptec controllers.  Thus you cannot have your boot device
attached to an adaptec Controller.  I would be surprised that once the
kernel is loaded OpenBSD would not find the Adaptec.

-- 
-- David    (obrien@NUXI.com)

